<title>JAPAN: CSK falls sharply after Sega suspension.</title>
<headline>CSK falls sharply after Sega suspension.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in CSK Corp, the largest shareholder of Sega Enterprises Ltd, fell sharply on the Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) on Friday after Sega shares were suspended, brokers said.  </p>
<p>Information service firm CSK has a 20 percent stake in Sega, which is an amusement equipment maker.</p>
<p>CSK shares were down 140 yen at 3,060 yen by 0546 GMT.</p>
<p>The TSE earlier halted trading in Sega shares for the rest of Friday because of unclear information about whether the company will revise its earnings forecast.</p>
<p>Sega said it would hold a news conference at 3.15 p.m. (0615 GMT).</p>
